  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One transaction, then a drain",
      "items": [
        "the optimistic row and the queued mutation are written in one transaction, so the UI promise and the pending work can never diverge",
        "the outbox is persisted and survives app restarts; the drain runs on reconnect, on foreground and from a background task",
        "the ViewModel owns the write; the View renders the pending row and never calls the network itself"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Settle or reject",
      "items": [
        "on success the server's answer is written and the row is settled, then the query prefix is invalidated — never refetch the world",
        "on failure the previous value is restored and the screen shows why; without the rollback it is data loss with a spinner",
        "the server wins a conflict: the local pending change is rejected visibly, never silently dropped"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Keys and fixtures",
      "items": [
        "every queued mutation carries an idempotency key, so a drained mutation sent twice is one mutation at the server",
        "the outbox is unit-tested with valid and invalid fixtures, like the parser and the quality governor",
        "the query cache is the last good data: offline is a visible state beside it, not a generic error"
      ]
    }
  ]
